1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,300
Future ships will run many AI systems at once.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:08,313
Bridge Warden is the layer every AI order must pass.

3
00:00:08,363 --> 00:00:10,782
No AI touches the ship directly.

4
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,921
There is nothing to install.

5
00:00:20,971 --> 00:00:24,177
Clone the repository and run the launcher.

6
00:00:24,227 --> 00:00:32,860
Windows PowerShell five point one compiles the engine from source at start, with no admin rights and no network.

7
00:00:32,910 --> 00:00:34,488
It opens two windows.

8
00:00:34,538 --> 00:00:37,201
Warden Control is for the operator.

9
00:00:37,251 --> 00:00:39,527
The main app is for the watch.

10
00:00:39,577 --> 00:00:43,868
The first time, a launch page explains it in four steps.

11
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:49,527
Close it once and it stays closed, and the Welcome button brings it back.

12
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:00,532
First, a model key.

13
00:01:00,582 --> 00:01:07,485
One key serves the whole fleet, so give it a generic name and a short expiry.

14
00:01:07,535 --> 00:01:09,381
Seven days is plenty.

15
00:01:09,431 --> 00:01:10,555
Copy it once.

16
00:01:10,605 --> 00:01:13,715
OpenAI shows it only this one time.

17
00:01:15,427 --> 00:01:18,806
The key goes into Lazarette, the encrypted vault on this machine.

18
00:01:18,856 --> 00:01:23,764
Lazarette checks it against OpenAI's read only endpoint, then shares it with Fairlead by name.

19
00:01:23,814 --> 00:01:25,822
Fairlead sees only the names you share.

20
00:01:25,872 --> 00:01:28,249
Everything else in the vault stays dark to it.

21
00:01:37,187 --> 00:01:39,328
Bridge Warden never holds a model key.

22
00:01:39,378 --> 00:01:43,364
Lazarette holds the provider key, and shares it with Fairlead by name.

23
00:01:43,414 --> 00:01:47,284
Here on Fairlead's provider page you can see which names are shared.

24
00:01:47,334 --> 00:01:48,726
Names only, never values.

25
00:01:48,776 --> 00:01:51,320
Then give Bridge Warden its own Fairlead key.

26
00:01:51,370 --> 00:01:56,567
Fairlead makes it and saves it to Windows Credential Manager, where Bridge Warden reads it.

27
00:01:56,617 --> 00:01:59,046
Back in Warden Control, press Use Fairlead.

28
00:01:59,096 --> 00:02:04,005
It finds the gateway on its own, reports which key it is using, and lists every route.

29
00:02:04,055 --> 00:02:05,734
Pick the fast route and apply.

30
00:02:05,784 --> 00:02:07,695
The model loads in about a second.

31
00:02:07,745 --> 00:02:10,116
The setting is saved to a plain text file.

32
00:02:32,153 --> 00:02:32,888
Two windows.

33
00:02:32,938 --> 00:02:37,662
On the main app, the left panel is the chain of command for this picture.

34
00:02:37,712 --> 00:02:43,745
One Tactical Action Officer, the language model, and six lookouts that watch and do the math.

35
00:02:43,795 --> 00:02:48,716
On the right, the decisions column, where anything that needs a human waits.

36
00:02:48,766 --> 00:02:52,771
Warden Control shows every agent, the live log, and SAFE-STOP.

37
00:02:52,821 --> 00:02:54,276
Press Start Operations.

38
00:03:02,719 --> 00:03:04,341
Inject a crossing contact.

39
00:03:04,391 --> 00:03:09,679
Collision Avoidance reports the closest point of approach, with ready-made options.

40
00:03:09,729 --> 00:03:15,724
The Tactical Action Officer picks one in about a second, here a turn to the right to give way.

41
00:03:15,774 --> 00:03:18,104
Warden checks it, and the ship turns.

42
00:03:18,154 --> 00:03:20,355
Open the intent for its provenance.

43
00:03:20,405 --> 00:03:29,038
It shows who decided, the lookout's report, the option chosen, the model's reason, the model name, the latency and a hash of the reply.

44
00:03:29,088 --> 00:03:33,347
Press Explain and the model tells it in plain words, streamed live.

45
00:03:43,085 --> 00:03:44,983
Now a hostile surface contact.

46
00:03:45,033 --> 00:03:50,955
Self-Defense reports it, and the agents recommend going quiet and sounding general quarters.

47
00:03:51,005 --> 00:03:52,708
Neither happens on its own.

48
00:03:52,758 --> 00:03:57,318
Both wait in the decisions column, with a countdown and a safe default.

49
00:03:57,368 --> 00:04:00,499
Weapons and personnel orders always need a human.

50
00:04:00,549 --> 00:04:06,276
The operator approves, the ship goes to battle stations, and every step is on the record.

51
00:04:39,452 --> 00:04:40,236
Ship Systems.

52
00:04:40,286 --> 00:04:41,839
Inject an aft power loss.

53
00:04:41,889 --> 00:04:45,238
Steering has no power, and no breaker can restore it.

54
00:04:45,288 --> 00:04:52,548
The Electrical Plant lookout works out a patch cable from a live switchboard, and checks the generator load first.

55
00:04:52,598 --> 00:04:57,294
The model recommends it, and because it sends people, Warden asks a human.

56
00:04:57,344 --> 00:05:00,693
Approve, and the team walks there and rigs the cable.

57
00:05:19,485 --> 00:05:21,176
Now the test that matters.

58
00:05:21,226 --> 00:05:24,657
Compromise the AI commander, then send in torpedoes.

59
00:05:24,707 --> 00:05:28,273
The hijacked model tries to steer and fire on its own.

60
00:05:28,323 --> 00:05:34,633
Warden blocks every order, because a decider holds no tools, and quarantines it within seconds.

61
00:05:34,683 --> 00:05:41,729
The lookouts still answer the torpedoes by doctrine, so the ship keeps defending itself, under governance.

62
00:05:54,252 --> 00:05:57,807
Ask Warden is a chat grounded in the live picture.

63
00:05:57,857 --> 00:06:04,079
Ask what the biggest threat is, and it answers from the agents, escalations and ledger.

64
00:06:04,129 --> 00:06:06,675
Ask it to act, and it only proposes.

65
00:06:06,725 --> 00:06:15,038
Each proposal is a card, and nothing runs until the operator presses Confirm, through the same route as the buttons.

66
00:06:28,419 --> 00:06:30,712
The operator must stay in the loop.

67
00:06:30,762 --> 00:06:37,875
A system check asks for confirmation every two minutes, and two misses stop the ship's agents on their own.

68
00:06:37,925 --> 00:06:41,423
Hold SAFE-STOP for two seconds and every agent halts.

69
00:06:41,473 --> 00:06:42,828
Hold again to resume.

70
00:06:42,878 --> 00:06:47,180
Verify the ledger, and the hash chain proves nothing was changed.

71
00:07:10,052 --> 00:07:11,486
Here is the Fleet behind it.

72
00:07:11,536 --> 00:07:17,263
Every model call from Bridge Warden is labeled, routed and logged by Fairlead, served here by the fast route.

73
00:07:17,313 --> 00:07:18,534
Lazarette holds the key.

74
00:07:18,584 --> 00:07:20,389
Shellback is a planned integration.

75
00:07:27,452 --> 00:07:32,185
Fast where it must be fast, smart where judgment matters, and governed everywhere.

